(3169945, 441828, 3746, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by whiterook:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by crazedfost78:</b></div><hr/><i> How did this picture win? Sorry but I am not as inspired here. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Ditto </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Let me explain, Alex submitted the photo for scoring, then for 7 days it was up to you, the viewer, to vote on it. The photo with the highest average vote wins the challenge. Its really quite straightforward and is the one thing DPC are still getting right these days.<br/> <br/>Hope this clears things up for you!!</td>', 'Originally posted by whiterook: Originally posted by crazedfost78: How did this picture win? Sorry but I am not as inspired here.   Ditto   Let me explain, Alex submitted the photo for scoring, then for 7 days it was up to you, the viewer, to vote on it. The photo with the highest average vote wins the challenge. Its really quite straightforward and is the one thing DPC are still getting right these days. Hope this clears things up for you!!', '2007-01-02 10:14:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(3170101, 442129, 58430, '<td valign="top">You take absolutely breathtaking pictures.  This image is amazing.  Color tones, silhouette, foreground looks like you are walking on water.  Lovely  images as well in the comment section.  I wish I was close enough to this location to take pictures like these.  Beautiful, really love them.<br/> <br/>All that being said, I am really tired of seeing this location in so many challenges.  You are so talented...can you drive somewhere else or hide the big rock?  I love the blue toned picture above and it does not wear me out because it does not look like the same old rock again and again and the blue color evokes an almost eerie moodiness.<br/> <br/>edit:  finish a couple sentences.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-01-02 10:58:07.</i></td>', 'You take absolutely breathtaking pictures.  This image is amazing.  Color tones, silhouette, foreground looks like you are walking on water.  Lovely  images as well in the comment section.  I wish I was close enough to this location to take pictures like these.  Beautiful, really love them. All that being said, I am really tired of seeing this location in so many challenges.  You are so talented...can you drive somewhere else or hide the big rock?  I love the blue toned picture above and it does not wear me out because it does not look like the same old rock again and again and the blue color evokes an almost eerie moodiness. edit:  finish a couple sentences.', '2007-01-02 10:56:25.000000', '2007-01-02 10:58:07.000000', 0),
