(3180741, 441398, 43410, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique club, my name is Jon Rowe, and i will be looking at your image this evening :)<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Lighting : </b> first of all let me say i''ve been a fan of your work for some time now, so ME critiquing your image seems odd, but i''m really glad to have the opportunity.  now, the composition on this shot is great, i like the slightly off-center comp.  when i look at this setup, i think of the broken world we live in, and the light that you''re helping to shine to it (hence your background).  this is just an amazing shot.  only thing i can possibly nit-pick is the very obvious vinette.  i gave it an 8.  loved this shot.<br/> <br/><b>Challenge : </b> it definitely fits the challenge.  every aspect of it is very emotive, yet has a humorous factor to it at the same time.  great job, and very well done.  it should have finished higher, in my opinion.<br/> <br/><b>Conclusion : </b> this is a very well done, and incredibly underrated photo.  everything from the lighting to the composition and execution just rocks for me.  i really like it.  if you were to take a break and lay your camera down for a while, i think that would be an injustice to both your talent and the DPC community, you do great work<br/> <br/>Keep on shootin!<br/> <br/>Good luck on your future challenges:)<br/>-Jon Rowe<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-01-04 13:02:09.</i></td>', 'Hello from the Critique club, my name is Jon Rowe, and i will be looking at your image this evening :) Composition/Lighting :  first of all let me say i''ve been a fan of your work for some time now, so ME critiquing your image seems odd, but i''m really glad to have the opportunity.  now, the composition on this shot is great, i like the slightly off-center comp.  when i look at this setup, i think of the broken world we live in, and the light that you''re helping to shine to it (hence your background).  this is just an amazing shot.  only thing i can possibly nit-pick is the very obvious vinette.  i gave it an 8.  loved this shot. Challenge :  it definitely fits the challenge.  every aspect of it is very emotive, yet has a humorous factor to it at the same time.  great job, and very well done.  it should have finished higher, in my opinion. Conclusion :  this is a very well done, and incredibly underrated photo.  everything from the lighting to the composition and execution just rocks for me.  i really like it.  if you were to take a break and lay your camera down for a while, i think that would be an injustice to both your talent and the DPC community, you do great work Keep on shootin! Good luck on your future challenges:)-Jon Rowe', '2007-01-04 13:01:19.000000', '2007-01-04 13:02:09.000000', 0),
(3180805, 442240, 43410, '<td valign="top">Comment:<br/>Hello from the Critique club, my name is Jon Rowe, and i will be looking at your image this evening :)<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Lighting : </b> i really think the composition and the lighting of this are spot on.  there''s a great amount of contrast to hold the attention, and the eye travels quite pleasingly throughout the image, with the main focus brought on that cute face with the wore out look :D  i feel your pain;)  great job on the lighting composition. as a fellow college student, i could not possibly tell you how i agree with this image.  only thing i was thinking was what someone else said about having more books open.  this would show more frustration and stress, and could have further showed your problems.  nonetheless, it''s a great image, and very nice score.  congrats on your new personal best :D<br/> <br/><b>Challenge : </b> it definitely fits the challenge quite well.  being a college student is definitely full time, and this really shows the aggrevation you go through.  <br/> <br/><b>Conclusion : </b> i love everything about this image.  great lighting, great execution.  everything is wonderful.  congratulations on a job well done :D<br/> <br/>Keep on shootin!<br/> <br/>Good luck on your future challenges:)<br/>-Jon Rowe</td>', 'Comment:Hello from the Critique club, my name is Jon Rowe, and i will be looking at your image this evening :) Composition/Lighting :  i really think the composition and the lighting of this are spot on.  there''s a great amount of contrast to hold the attention, and the eye travels quite pleasingly throughout the image, with the main focus brought on that cute face with the wore out look :D  i feel your pain;)  great job on the lighting composition. as a fellow college student, i could not possibly tell you how i agree with this image.  only thing i was thinking was what someone else said about having more books open.  this would show more frustration and stress, and could have further showed your problems.  nonetheless, it''s a great image, and very nice score.  congrats on your new personal best :D Challenge :  it definitely fits the challenge quite well.  being a college student is definitely full time, and this really shows the aggrevation you go through.   Conclusion :  i love everything about this image.  great lighting, great execution.  everything is wonderful.  congratulations on a job well done :D Keep on shootin! Good luck on your future challenges:)-Jon Rowe', '2007-01-04 13:13:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(3180849, 440202, 43410, '<td valign="top">Comment:<br/>Hello from the Critique club, my name is Jon Rowe, and i will be looking at your image this evening :)<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Lighting : </b> this is a very interesting image.  i like it a lot.  it really has a lot of potential.  i think the composition works, and the cluttered background truly shows the life of an IT specialist.  i''ve worked in computer repair / IT for 6 years now, and this looks like my desk :D  i think the monitor should definitely be on, w/ maybe a blue screen to fit the rest of the image, and might have given some additional fill light from behind.  lighting is on, but maybe a slightly faster shutter speed to get rid of those blown highlights on the right side.<br/> <br/><b>Challenge : </b>  i think this fits the challenge quite nicely.  it really caught my eye when voting b/c i can relate to it, and i think it shows how busy the profession is, wether it''s helping out a customer or killing time on DPC between jobs :D  very well done.<br/> <br/><b>Conclusion : </b> composition, lighting, all is well done.  just a few things w/ blowouts here and there, but other than that well done.  very nice score on this, and as you continue to enter more challenges, i think the potential you have here will prove well for you, and you''ll continue to grow as a photographer.  very nice job!<br/> <br/>Keep on shootin!<br/> <br/>Good luck on your future challenges:)<br/>-Jon Rowe</td>', 'Comment:Hello from the Critique club, my name is Jon Rowe, and i will be looking at your image this evening :) Composition/Lighting :  this is a very interesting image.  i like it a lot.  it really has a lot of potential.  i think the composition works, and the cluttered background truly shows the life of an IT specialist.  i''ve worked in computer repair / IT for 6 years now, and this looks like my desk :D  i think the monitor should definitely be on, w/ maybe a blue screen to fit the rest of the image, and might have given some additional fill light from behind.  lighting is on, but maybe a slightly faster shutter speed to get rid of those blown highlights on the right side. Challenge :   i think this fits the challenge quite nicely.  it really caught my eye when voting b/c i can relate to it, and i think it shows how busy the profession is, wether it''s helping out a customer or killing time on DPC between jobs :D  very well done. Conclusion :  composition, lighting, all is well done.  just a few things w/ blowouts here and there, but other than that well done.  very nice score on this, and as you continue to enter more challenges, i think the potential you have here will prove well for you, and you''ll continue to grow as a photographer.  very nice job! Keep on shootin! Good luck on your future challenges:)-Jon Rowe', '2007-01-04 13:18:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(3180880, 442299, 43410, '<td valign="top">Comment:<br/>Hello from the Critique club, my name is Jon Rowe, and i will be looking at your image this evening :)<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Lighting : </b> the lighting on this is quite well, but i believe that i would have tried a different angle to get rid of the finger''s shadow.  i really like the slight desaturation of this image.  it works well.  i believe i would have cloned out that strat thread on your sleeve there as well.<br/> <br/><b>Challenge : </b> this fits the challenge well.  the woody subject is either a love hate relationship among the voters, so it sometimes is a chance to use, but it think it worked well for you here.<br/> <br/><b>Conclusion : </b> image overall is done well, just think about those few things i said and what others commented on as well.  you did a great job.  you should be proud of this image<br/> <br/>Keep on shootin!<br/> <br/>Good luck on your future challenges:)<br/>-Jon Rowe</td>', 'Comment:Hello from the Critique club, my name is Jon Rowe, and i will be looking at your image this evening :) Composition/Lighting :  the lighting on this is quite well, but i believe that i would have tried a different angle to get rid of the finger''s shadow.  i really like the slight desaturation of this image.  it works well.  i believe i would have cloned out that strat thread on your sleeve there as well. Challenge :  this fits the challenge well.  the woody subject is either a love hate relationship among the voters, so it sometimes is a chance to use, but it think it worked well for you here. Conclusion :  image overall is done well, just think about those few things i said and what others commented on as well.  you did a great job.  you should be proud of this image Keep on shootin! Good luck on your future challenges:)-Jon Rowe', '2007-01-04 13:21:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(3180927, 440229, 43410, '<td valign="top">Comment:<br/>Hello from the Critique club, my name is Jon Rowe, and i will be looking at your image this evening :)<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Lighting : </b> the lighting in this image really seems to be great.  you have the main light at the right angle, and the shadows on the opposite side are very nice, w/out losing detail.  as i stated when voting, this image is incredibly too small.  if it was tripled in size, more detail would have come through.  i''m afraid that when an image is submitted this small, voters dont'' waste their time and just vote it low b/c of the size.  crystal left you a great link to a tutorial, if you use that in your next challenge, i believe you will have better luck w/ the voters.<br/> <br/><b>Challenge : </b> this is very humorous.  if he''s retired, i can see how this would fit the challenge.  it shows his relaxing, and enjoying his time off after years of hard work.  but, i have to guess if he''s retired due to the lack of detail due to the small picture size<br/> <br/><b>Conclusion : </b> overall it''s a very good image, that was lit very nicely.  if this took full advantage of the pixel dimensions, i think this would have been a 5.5 - 6 image easily.  good luck, and let me know if you have any questions about my critique.<br/> <br/>Keep on shootin!<br/> <br/>Good luck on your future challenges:)<br/>-Jon Rowe</td>', 'Comment:Hello from the Critique club, my name is Jon Rowe, and i will be looking at your image this evening :) Composition/Lighting :  the lighting in this image really seems to be great.  you have the main light at the right angle, and the shadows on the opposite side are very nice, w/out losing detail.  as i stated when voting, this image is incredibly too small.  if it was tripled in size, more detail would have come through.  i''m afraid that when an image is submitted this small, voters dont'' waste their time and just vote it low b/c of the size.  crystal left you a great link to a tutorial, if you use that in your next challenge, i believe you will have better luck w/ the voters. Challenge :  this is very humorous.  if he''s retired, i can see how this would fit the challenge.  it shows his relaxing, and enjoying his time off after years of hard work.  but, i have to guess if he''s retired due to the lack of detail due to the small picture size Conclusion :  overall it''s a very good image, that was lit very nicely.  if this took full advantage of the pixel dimensions, i think this would have been a 5.5 - 6 image easily.  good luck, and let me know if you have any questions about my critique. Keep on shootin! Good luck on your future challenges:)-Jon Rowe', '2007-01-04 13:28:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(3181300, 441577, 44490, '<td valign="top">Aimee, congratulations on another high finish and an honorable mention.  Good portrait, fitting pose, expression, eye contact, props.  Thanks for your care of the Earth.  Blessings from your "arts &amp; crafts" kindred spirit.<br/></td>', 'Aimee, congratulations on another high finish and an honorable mention.  Good portrait, fitting pose, expression, eye contact, props.  Thanks for your care of the Earth.  Blessings from your "arts & crafts" kindred spirit.', '2007-01-04 15:13:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(3181414, 442215, 48389, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club and a Happy New Year Giorgio!</b> <br/> <br/>Congratulations on your Top 10 finish!<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/> <br/>I\''m not sure how to critique this image! I think your composition is excellent. Your pose really made me laugh, definitely that of someone who needs a change of career!<br/> <br/><b>Technicals:</b> <br/> <br/>The HDR effect you have going here really suits the image and with the leafless trees the colours and tones your post processing has given really make the image come to life! Not really a lot else I can say about this!<br/> <br/>Sorry for such a short critique!<br/> <br/>If you\''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>- Natalya :o)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-01-04 15:52:00.</i></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club and a Happy New Year Giorgio!  Congratulations on your Top 10 finish! Composition:  I\''m not sure how to critique this image! I think your composition is excellent. Your pose really made me laugh, definitely that of someone who needs a change of career! Technicals:  The HDR effect you have going here really suits the image and with the leafless trees the colours and tones your post processing has given really make the image come to life! Not really a lot else I can say about this! Sorry for such a short critique! If you\''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. - Natalya :o)', '2007-01-04 15:40:55.000000', '2007-01-04 15:52:00.000000', 0),
(3181522, 441358, 48389, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club Shez!!</b> <br/> <br/>I am not sure I can say anything other that FANTASTIC!! A beautiful composition with wonderful colours that just pull the viewer in! I suppose the one and only ''negative'' thing I can say about the image is that ''technically'' (to all the DNMC voters) this doesn''t strictly meet the challenge title. But, that said, your explanation tells us straight away the reason why this SHOULD fit the challenge!<br/> <br/>Another lovely image from a lovely lady. Thank you for sharing this :o)<br/> <br/>- Natalya :o)</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club Shez!!  I am not sure I can say anything other that FANTASTIC!! A beautiful composition with wonderful colours that just pull the viewer in! I suppose the one and only ''negative'' thing I can say about the image is that ''technically'' (to all the DNMC voters) this doesn''t strictly meet the challenge title. But, that said, your explanation tells us straight away the reason why this SHOULD fit the challenge! Another lovely image from a lovely lady. Thank you for sharing this :o) - Natalya :o)', '2007-01-04 16:10:02.000000', NULL, 0),
